        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 88.16" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="604" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis de uulnere, quod alicui fecerit, componere uelit, ita componat, ut precium uulneris in precium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#Hn_88-16.lnote.oe.35"/> were numeretur, si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="l" target="#Hn_88-16.lnote.oe.l"/> homo mortuus inde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#Hn_88-16.lnote.oe.36"/> sit.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 604 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
